@mdblack98 I've got a question regarding the `?` (question mark) responses from Yaesu rigs: It seems the error responses for Yaesu rigs are not really documented anywhere and the interpretation that a question mark would indicate the rig being "busy" originates from some Kenwood code -- am I correct here?

Based on my tests, FTDX101, FTDX 5000 and FT-991 use the `?` response to indicate that the command parameter isn't valid (e.g. invalid memory channel number) or that the command is not supported in the current mode (e.g. IF shift or NR level in FM mode on a FT-991). Retrying the command never helps in these cases and the "command timed out" error code used currently is misleading.

I was wondering if we should simply change the `?` to indicate `RIG_ERJCTED`, which IMO would be the correct interpretation as the use of this response seems to be (at least somewhat) consistent across Yaesu rigs.

